.FILL
^THE ^I^M^P72 COMPILER WAS DESIGNED AND IMPLEMENTED AT THE ^YALE
^UNIVERSITY ^DEPARTMENT OF ^COMPUTER ^SCIENCE BY ^WALT ^BILOFSKY, BASED LARGELY ON
PREVIOUS WORK OF ^E. ^T. ^IRONS.  ^SUBSTANTIAL CONTRIBUTIONS WERE MADE BY ^STEVEN
^WEINGART AND ^TERRY ^LYONS.  ^THIS MANUAL DESCRIBES VERSION 0.10.0 OF THE
^I^M^P72 COMPILER, WHICH TRANSLATES ^I^M^P72 TO NATIVE CODE ON 64-BIT ^UNIX SYSTEMS.

.SUBTITLE 1: ^INTRODUCTION.
.PAGE
.RIGHT MARGIN 60
.SKIP 3
.NOFILL
